+/* The three immutable plane buffers remain borrowed until release(user,index),
+ * exactly once after successful admission, including replacement/cancellation,
+ * render/sink failure and shutdown. A failed offer retains nothing and does not
+ * call release. The descriptor is copied; the samples are not. The same byte
+ * limit and latest-pending policy apply. release runs without queue locks on
+ * a producer, worker or cancelling thread, possibly before offer returns.
+ * It may query stats but must not offer/flush/finish/destroy this queue.
+ * flush/finish wait for all admitted leases' release callbacks to return.
+ * Callback context must remain alive through finish/destroy; callbacks must
+ * return cooperatively. A thrown release callback latches callback failure. */
